  "id": "behavior-hierarchy",
  "term": "behavior hierarchy",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, a behavior hierarchy is the idea that action is shaped through an ordered chain of influences, with personal values affecting attitudes and norms, which then guide behavioral intentions. It describes behavior as the outcome of higher-level psychological factors rather than a stand-alone act.",
